# MineWorldCraft launch settings for Robinhood Chain (public values only: never put the Crafters reveal secret or any
# private key here). Used by script/deploy-mainnet.sh.
#
# $MINE: Courier World's $STAMP under another name (MineToken is StampToken line for line). Capped at 21,000,000,
# counting every mint, so burns are permanent. At the launch 10,500,000 is minted to the pool hook and locked for good
# as liquidity in the $MINE/IMD pool; the rest is minted only by the mining vault (MineVault, its one minter, set once)
# as players claim what they earned: at most 35,000 a day and 10,500,000 in all, so it takes at least 300 days. The
# deploy then renounces the token: no owner, no proxy, no pause, no blocklist, no transfer tax (the 4% trading fee is
# the hook's, and the hook is renounced too, so the fee recipient is final). Upgrades and shop payments burn part of
# what they cost, so the supply that exists only ever shrinks from what was minted.

# Owns every contract that has an owner: the vault, the MiningSites, MinePayments and CrafterLevels proxies (the owner
# tunes the game and can upgrade those three) and the Crafters. The deploying wallet may be another one: it sets the
# owner at deploy, and prints any call only the owner can then make (acceptOwnership, setAttributesExtension...).
# Hand it to a multisig or a timelock later with transferOwnership (two steps), if you like.
OWNER=0x6e85Dc9f094b7DD35a2A981AbBd0AC9C496670eD
# Receives the 4% trading fee on every $MINE swap (paid in IMD).
FEE_RECIPIENT=0x6e85Dc9f094b7DD35a2A981AbBd0AC9C496670eD
# Receives mining site sales (ETH), what isn't burned of upgrades and payments ($MINE), Crafters mint payments (if the
# mint ever has a price) and the Crafters' 5% royalty. Defaults to FEE_RECIPIENT.
TREASURY=0x6e85Dc9f094b7DD35a2A981AbBd0AC9C496670eD
# Launch price as a fully diluted market cap for all 21M $MINE, in US dollars (converted to IMD at deploy time from the
# IMD/ETH pool and Chainlink ETH/USD). The pool holds 10.5M of them.
START_MCAP_USD=5000

# MiningSites (the rules for converting earnings; upgradeable): ETH to open a site (0.005 ETH, in wei), and the daily
# caps on the $MINE it has minted, in $MINE wei: 1,500 per wallet and 35,000 across everyone. The owner can change them
# later, up to 3,500 per wallet and 35,000 across everyone. Whatever runs in MiningSites, the vault never mints more than
# 35,000 a day (fixed forever), so its 10,500,000 can't all be minted in under 300 days (earnings a site's rate doesn't
# convert are never minted, so it lasts longer still).
SITE_PRICE=5000000000000000
WALLET_DAILY_CAP=1500000000000000000000
DAILY_CAP=35000000000000000000000
# A site opens at level 1 and converts 50% of its earnings; upgrades (upgradeSite, paid in $MINE) raise it to 60%, 70%,
# 85% and 100% at levels 2 to 5. Default costs to reach levels 2, 3, 4 and 5: 4,620, 18,942, 77,662 and 318,415 $MINE
# (about $11 for the first, $1,000 for all four at a $50,000 market cap), 75% of each burned, 25% to the treasury. The
# owner can later change the costs (setUpgradeCosts, each 1 wei to 1,000,000 $MINE), the rates (setRates, each 10% to
# 100%, never lower for a higher level), the burn share (setUpgradeBurnBps, 0-100%), and add levels (addLevel, up to
# 20). To launch with other costs, list four amounts in $MINE wei:
# SITE_UPGRADE_COSTS=4620000000000000000000,18942000000000000000000,77662000000000000000000,318415000000000000000000
# The game server's voucher key signs claims. Pass its ADDRESS (never the key) when launching:
#   MINING_SIGNER=0x... ./script/deploy-mainnet.sh launch --broadcast --browser --browser-disable-open
# (or set it here once it exists). The key itself only goes into the multiplayer Worker's secrets.
# MINING_SIGNER=

# MinePayments (upgradeable): what players pay the game in $MINE, at the game's own prices. Kinds at launch: 0 "shop"
# (75% burned, 25% to the treasury) and 1 "ticket" (all to the treasury). The owner can change a kind's burn share and
# add kinds (setKindBurn, addKind). Deployed with the launch.

# MineWorld Crafters (3,333 on-chain pixel-art characters): the mint price in wei per Crafter (0: free at launch; the
# owner can set one later with setPrice, paid straight to the treasury), how many one wallet can mint in all (1-50,
# setWalletLimit), and the transfer validator that enforces the 5% royalty (OpenSea's creator fee enforcement
# registry). OWNER owns the collection (and reveals it with the secret).
CRAFTERS_PRICE=0
CRAFTERS_WALLET_LIMIT=10
CRAFTERS_VALIDATOR=0xA000027A9B2802E1ddf7000061001e5c005A0000
# Optional: the collection's website and social links, and its picture and banner on OpenSea (URLs; OpenSea doesn't
# take data: URIs for these). The owner can set or change them at any time with setLinks(website, social) and
# setCollectionImages(image, banner), sold out or not, so they can wait until the domain and accounts exist. (Setting
# any of these here, or a wallet limit other than 10, has the deploying wallet set them up first; then OWNER accepts
# the collection with acceptOwnership.)
# CRAFTERS_WEBSITE=https://mineworldcraft.fun/
# CRAFTERS_SOCIAL=https://x.com/...
# CRAFTERS_IMAGE=https://mineworldcraft.fun/crafters/collection.png
# CRAFTERS_BANNER=https://mineworldcraft.fun/crafters/banner.png

# Crafter levels (CrafterLevels, upgradeable): every Crafter starts at level 1; its holder upgrades it to level 5 with
# $MINE (75% burned, 25% to the treasury), and the level stays with the token when it's sold. Default costs to reach
# levels 2, 3, 4 and 5: 2,310, 9,471, 38,831 and 159,207 $MINE (half a site's: about $500 for all four at a $50,000
# market cap). The owner can later change the costs (each 1 wei to 2,000,000 $MINE) and the burn share, and add levels
# (up to 20). The Crafters show the level as a trait once their owner points them at it
# (setAttributesExtension(levels)). To launch with other costs:
# CRAFTER_UPGRADE_COSTS=2310000000000000000000,9471000000000000000000,38831000000000000000000,159207000000000000000000
# CrafterLevels needs both $MINE and the Crafters. If the Crafters are deployed first, put their address here and the
# launch deploys CrafterLevels too; otherwise run `./script/deploy-mainnet.sh levels` after both (it reads the
# addresses from deployments/). Either way the deploy points the Crafters at it if the deploying wallet owns them, and
# otherwise prints the setAttributesExtension call for OWNER.
# CRAFTERS=0x...
